# Every source change since the replay rig — one commit at a time

Generated by `scripts/gen_rig_diff.sh`; regenerate after adding commits.
Base: `7eaaa63` (2026-09-03), the first TESTS.md.

The rig itself, docs and scripts are excluded — this is what the GAME does
differently. `docs/TESTS.md` has the reasoning and the asm citations; this
file is the code, so a change can be reviewed without going commit hunting.

CLASS says whether a commit can alter **Amiga-mode play**, which is what the
game ships in and what the DOS corpus cannot test:

  AMIGA  changes shipped play — the reviewable surface
  DOS    behind `_gDosGameplay`, Amiga arm byte-identical
  VIEW   a literal rewritten as f(view); identical at 336x272
  FLAG   behind an opt-in -D; default build unchanged
  RIG    inert unless --replay-test
  NOOP   no behaviour change

