- `22f370a` fix: onScreen culled to the render width, and was overwrit — splits onScreen from the render cull and pins the sim view to 336
- `2247d74` sim: four more bugs the sprite level found, and the bench  — ball-quadrant leading bound + clr.w on sprite z (SetBallPosition)
- `6ce24b7` sim: five "nearest player" scans walked the sprite table b — five nearest-player scans now walk the table forwards
- `e24f55f` goalie: the catch gate read GoalieSkill offsets 0 and 2, n — goalie catch reads GoalieSkill 0x2A/0x2C; tackling timer >= -2
- `f337e13` tactics: the DOS "rewritten forward rows" are dead data � — InitUserTactics writes through _teamTacticsTable; no-op by default
- `04f8f01` ai: three fire gates in AI_SetControlsDirection read the w — AI fire gates, angle tolerance, dead $FFFF arm, 478 bound
- `b5b850c` ai: a block the DOS build does not have, and a register th — a2 is the ball (parameter, not a local); CPU-only position block
- `9a7bc65` pass: a `tst.l` on a two-byte field spans the next one — tst.l spans longPass+longSpinPass in three tests
- `24159a6` tackle: four shifts, not five — the comment said /32 and — near-goal slowdown is four shifts (/16), not five
- `7a08d16` controls: the AI team's tackle clears PLAYER 1's fire coun — an AI tackle clears pl1FireCounter (shared asm tail)
- `6c1aa1a` timers: a held fire button froze the stoppage countdown — unmatched end-game state falls through to the stoppage countdown
- `59a65a1` ball: the goalpost deflection has three arms, and the port — goalpost deflection has three arms
- `310c1a6` anim: sprites in the widescreen margin were drawn but neve — animation follows the render view (widescreen only)
- `28f8204` camera: the widescreen camera stopped 148px short and left — camera pan range is the simulation constant, not the render width
- `97dd23a` camera: split the render origin from the game camera — t — render origin split from the game camera (widescreen only)
- `0624126` hud: the score panel and the match clock anchored on the w — HUD + bench menus anchor on the render origin (widescreen only)

