+ * its 350 coverage bytes, Sweep in 64 and 4-3-3 in 10 — 142 of 4200 in all.
+ * 3-4-3 needs a variant here only because THIS PORT changed it (see
+ * SWOS_ORIGINAL_TACTICS above); the DOS 3-4-3 is the pristine Amiga one.
+ *
+ * The 4-4-2 and Sweep deltas are not the nudges the byte counts suggest: 60 of
+ * the 4-4-2's 68 and 61 of Sweep's 64 are the two FORWARD slots, rewritten
+ * rather than adjusted — DOS keeps the strikers in a narrow central channel
+ * where the Amiga spreads them wide. Everything outside those two slots is
+ * single-byte changes, one per slot.
+ *
+ * WHY: `ApplyGameStyle` (dos_gameplay.c) switches the physics and timer
+ * constants for DOS gameplay but not the formations, and `GetPlayerPrice`
+ * walks the tactics table for every player — so DOS mode was deriving Amiga
